From 506ffff3f2b9497a79142fd5ab73f6d688fc74f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
by: triplecN
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] shunko: exclude connected peers, rotate targets; warn on a
 slow clock

rpc/mempool: the addrman candidate path could return this node's own outbound
peer, and the empty-addrman fallback used outbound peers only. Both defeat the
one-shot-connection premise; connected peers are now excluded and an empty
candidate set is an honest error. Auto-selected targets rotate through a
16-entry recent list so one receiver cannot profile every hand-over. Explicit
targets are unchanged.

validation: the once-per-refusal log pointer was a function-local static that
outlived its Chainstate and leaked into the next one; it is a Chainstate member
now.

node/chainstate: warn when the tip is more than MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME (10 min)
but less than TIMESTAMP_WINDOW (2 h) ahead, where start-up passes but consensus
rejects every new block until the clock is fixed.

fuzz: per_ticket_deserialize feeds raw bytes straight into the ticket
deserializer and checks the round trip.
---
 src/node/chainstate.cpp | 10 +++++++
 src/rpc/mempool.cpp     | 59 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 src/test/fuzz/per.cpp   | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/validation.cpp      |  9 +++----
 src/validation.h        |  5 ++++
 5 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/node/chainstate.cpp b/src/node/chainstate.cpp
